        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^2-2x-1=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1\\pm\\sqrt{2}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-2x&=1\\\\x^2-2x+1&=2\\\\(x-1)^2&=2\\\\x-1&=\\pm\\sqrt{2}\\\\x&=1\\pm\\sqrt{2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$2x^2+5x=4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{-5\\pm\\sqrt{57}}{4}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2x^2+5x-4&=0\\\\b^2-4ac&=5^2-4(2)(-4)\\\\b^2-4ac&=57\\\\x&=\\frac{-5\\pm\\sqrt{57}}{2(2)}\\\\x&=\\frac{-5\\pm\\sqrt{57}}{4}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$4x^2-x-1=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{1\\pm\\sqrt{17}}{8}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}b^2-4ac&=(-1)^2-4(4)(-1)\\\\b^2-4ac&=17\\\\x&=\\frac{-(-1)\\pm\\sqrt{17}}{2(4)}\\\\x&=\\frac{1\\pm\\sqrt{17}}{8}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q4-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1}{x}=\\dfrac{x-1}{4}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{1\\pm\\sqrt{17}}{2}$",
          "worked": "$x\\ne0$. Cross-multiply.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}4&=x(x-1)\\\\x^2-x-4&=0\\\\b^2-4ac&=(-1)^2-4(1)(-4)\\\\b^2-4ac&=17\\\\x&=\\frac{1\\pm\\sqrt{17}}{2}\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth values satisfy the denominator restriction.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 49
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q4-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{2x-1}{5}=\\dfrac{1}{3x+2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1$ or $x=-\\dfrac{7}{6}$",
          "worked": "$x\\ne-\\frac{2}{3}$. Cross-multiply and factorise by splitting the middle term.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(2x-1)(3x+2)&=5\\\\6x^2+x-2&=5\\\\6x^2+x-7&=0\\\\6x^2+7x-6x-7&=0\\\\x(6x+7)-(6x+7)&=0\\\\(x-1)(6x+7)&=0\\\\x-1&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad6x+7=0\\\\x&=1\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=-\\frac{7}{6}\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth values satisfy the denominator restriction.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q4-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{2x+1}{5}=\\dfrac{-x}{3x-2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{1}{3}$ or $x=-1$",
          "worked": "$x\\ne\\frac{2}{3}$. Cross-multiply and factorise by splitting the middle term.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(2x+1)(3x-2)&=-5x\\\\6x^2-x-2&=-5x\\\\6x^2+4x-2&=0\\\\3x^2+2x-1&=0\\\\3x^2+3x-x-1&=0\\\\3x(x+1)-(x+1)&=0\\\\(3x-1)(x+1)&=0\\\\3x-1&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x+1=0\\\\x&=\\frac{1}{3}\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=-1\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth values satisfy the denominator restriction.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      }
